+- Results: Required formatting, module tidy, full tests, race detector, vet, focused local-development artifact static test, installed optional lint, vulnerability scan, static analysis, and snapshot release build passed. `goimports` is not installed in this environment.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups: No runtime API or persistence behavior changed. Future documentation stories should keep the markdown artifact, SECURITY.md verification gate row, CI step, verify step, and static release test synchronized.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Documentation stories can be made production-grade by treating markdown as a versioned contract and pinning exact commands, redaction rules, expected outputs, and gate wiring in `internal/release`.
+  - Static doc tests use simple substring checks, so required phrases should stay contiguous in Markdown when they are part of the contract.
